{
 "id": "2026-xu-cyclists",
 "name": "Cyclists' Perceived Safety and Comfort",
 "description": "Rebuilt from the published description of Xu, Luo, Delbosc, O'Hern & Chen (2026). Participants imagine cycling in 360° street panoramas from Gusu District, Suzhou, and pick the safer street of each pair, then the more comfortable one, using the paper's definitions of safety and comfort. Scores are TrueSkill ratings, as in the paper. Differences from the original study: (1) The paper reports about 30 votes per participant across both criteria but not how they were split or ordered; here each participant makes 15 safety then 15 comfort choices. (2) The paper's participant guideline (its Appendix 7.3) is not in the author version; the intro text on cycle lane types is written from the paper's description. (3) The background questions are short versions of the paper's recruitment criteria, not its wording. (4) Bundled images are 10 panoramas from the paper's figures (author version, CC BY), not the original 300-image set.",
